WEBVTT

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:33.690
<i>Having decided to climb Mt. Fuji,</i>

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:36.650
Plan for Climbing Mt. Fuji

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:36.650
<i>we put together a sensible plan.</i>

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:38.800
Let's review the schedule!

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:42.950
We'll depart Hanno Station at 6 AM,

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:47.870
then catch the highway bus leaving 
Shinjuku at 7:40 for Mt. Fuji 5th Station.

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:45.580
5th Station

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:51.670
6th Station

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:50.970
Let's see... our estimated 
arrival time is after 10 AM.

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:53.390
After letting ourselves 
acclimate there for a while,

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:53.250
 6th Station

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.500
 

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:54.760
we'll begin our climb.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:54.800
 8th Station

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:56.720
 

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:58.680
 8th Station

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:58.680
We'll stay overnight in a mountain 
hut at the Original 8th Station...

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.680
Summit

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:00.220
8th Station

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:01.800
Original 8th Station

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:02.930
Summit

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:02.290
and then set out before dawn.

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:05.680
Finally, we'll watch the 
sunrise from the summit.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:05.680
Summit

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:07.060
Does that sound fine?

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:08.350
Okay by me!

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:11.240
It sounds like a reasonable plan.

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:12.440
I think it's great.

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:16.490
Okay, I'll book reservations 
for the bus and mountain hut!

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:17.240
Mountain Trail

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:18.150
Season 2 - New Climb 8

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:20.490
Season 2 - New Climb 8 
 Make Lovely Memories

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:30.020
U-Um, I'd like to make a reservation.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:34.360
Uh, right, for four people!

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:35.680
The date is...

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:38.970
<i>So I took care of getting 
the preparations in order.</i>

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:43.280
<i>And now, tomorrow is the day 
when we'll finally climb Mt. Fuji!</i>

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:43.970
Bye bye!

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.250
Aoi! Are you all prepared?

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:47.980
I'm mostly ready.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:49.200
That reminds me,

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.690
don't I need to bring food?

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:53.830
Why would you?

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:56.070
You'll just get fat if you eat a lot.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:57.300
That's true.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:58.280
Are you nuts?!{she makes a pun on 'amai'(sweet, but also naive/soft)}

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:03.420
That idea of yours is nuttier than trail mix!

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.700
Calories are crucial!{the term she's using, 'koudoushoku' is a mountaineering/adventuring term for portable snacks; something a bit jargony would be perfect}{Ka: I couldn't find anything jargony enough for snacks here - MRE is a meal, GORP is too specific; I'm rewriting dialogue to avoid the "What's that word?" issue}

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:07.860
What do you mean?

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:09.660
You need snacks.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:10.790
Listen...

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.770
The energy you expend in one 
day of mountain climbing

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:17.300
can range from 4000 to 5000 kilocalories.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:20.290
That's equivalent to thirty rice balls!

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:22.680
Thirty?!

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:26.430
Consider this: What happens 
when a car runs out of gas?

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.390
It stops.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:31.770
Exactly! And we're the same way!

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:34.760
If a human exercises for 
too long without eating,

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:36.790
they will also end up stopping.

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:39.200
I-I see...

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.780
It's called "hitting the wall."{literally 'hunger knock'}

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:44.420
When you get too hungry, your blood sugar drops,

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:46.810
until you can't even take a single step.

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:51.120
That's why you have to eat 
frequently to avoid getting hungry.

00:03:54.470 --> 00:03:58.500
<i>So that's why Kaede-san gave 
me chocolate at Mt. Mitsutouge.</i>

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:03.840
<i>I... still don't know a thing 
about mountain climbing.</i>

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:07.420
<i>I was completely exhausted 
at Mt. Mitsutouge too.</i>

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:09.850
<i>Will I be able to handle this climb?</i>

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:15.250
Um... I was planning on using 
this trip as a Mt. Fuji diet...

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:16.730
Guess not?

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:18.730
Hinata-chan!

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:21.780
It's <i>not</i> cute to lose weight unhealthily!

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:26.980
Eating a lot and exercising a lot 
is the best shortcut to weight loss!

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:33.160
That statement's too persuasive 
coming from you, Kaede-san.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:37.020
Buy snacks to bring that are 
as sweet and tasty as possible!

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:38.560
Uh, right!

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:41.210
It's also a good idea to bring small change.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:44.300
It's handy for buying things, 
or going to use the restroom.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.680
If you're unsure about anything, give me a call!

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:47.820
See you tomorrow!

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:48.970
Okay!

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:49.950
Aoi!

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:53.630
Let's get going and buy some snacks!

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:54.790
Oh, sure!

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.730
I know! Let's invite Kokona-chan along!

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:00.230
I wonder what would be good...

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:01.480
Rice Crackers

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:02.730
Fruit Gummies

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:02.730
Gummies!

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:04.490
Chocolate peanuts sound good too!

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:06.240
Popcorn

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.240
I'm getting brown sugar puffs!

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:07.880
Brown sugar puffs?

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:09.650
You're like an old man.

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:11.640
I'll get dried fruit!

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:12.750
Sweet bean jelly!

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:17.040
Sweet
 Bean
 Jelly

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:15.550
You really are like an old man.

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:17.040
Hey, it's good stuff!

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:21.260
Since we'll be sweating, 
we should get salty snacks too.

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:22.110
Yeah.

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:25.010
Potato chips sound good too!

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:27.180
Sarara Wrap

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.180
Sarara Wrap

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:29.180
And also, this!

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:32.770
Kaede-san told me these come in handy.

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:36.590
Putting your snacks in them beforehand 
makes them easier to eat and reduces trash.

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:37.940
I see!

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:41.650
All Bottled Drinks 98 yen

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:41.650
We have our snacks, so I 
guess we just need liquids.

00:05:41.890 --> 00:05:44.160
Can't you buy them at Mt. Fuji?

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:47.530
The guidebook says they 
have them for sale there,

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:50.910
but the prices rise with the elevation.

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:54.460
Also, the ground at Mt. Fuji 
ends up soaking up all the rain,

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:56.760
so there are no rivers or springs.

00:05:57.910 --> 00:06:00.110
And so, to avoid exhaustion,

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:02.170
we should pack some liquids too.

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:02.170
Lemon Tea

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:03.310
Right!

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:06.800
Then, I'll get a sports drink.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:08.040
And you, Hinata?

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:10.510
I already got mine.

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:11.930
Roasted green tea!

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:13.890
When did you pick that up?

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:16.060
Bean Jelly - Brown Sugar Puffs

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.060
You sure you're not an old man?

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:23.020
It looks like we'll have good 
weather tomorrow, thank goodness.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:23.570
Yeah!

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:26.070
Perfect climbing weather.

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:35.540
<i>I'm...</i>

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:37.700
<i>feeling anxious again.</i>

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:42.420
<i>Will I... be able to handle the climb tomorrow?</i>

00:06:42.850 --> 00:06:44.030
Aoi-san?

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:45.820
You all right?

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:49.640
Uh, yeah! I'm fine, just a bit tired.

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:52.430
<i>I answered by reflex...</i>

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:56.260
Okay, it's time to get packed 
for tomorrow, so let's go home!

00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:57.770
You're right.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:01.410
Aoi-san, please have a good rest.

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:03.560
Sure. Thank you.

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:06.860
<i>I brought up the whole idea in the first place.</i>

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:11.610
<i>I shouldn't burden Hinata and 
Kokona-chan with my worries.</i>

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:13.240
<i>But...</i>

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:16.080
S-Say!

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:19.580
Uh, well...

00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:24.290
To tell you the truth, I'm worried about 
whether I'll be able to handle the climb.

00:07:26.270 --> 00:07:27.550
No kidding.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:29.460
I'm a little worried myself.

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:30.720
So am I.

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:34.390
But, since it's all been decided,

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:36.810
I can't go against the momentum!

00:07:37.150 --> 00:07:39.470
I'm anxious, but also looking forward to it.

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:40.230
Right!

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:41.970
<i>I see!</i>

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:44.440
<i>We all feel the same way!</i>

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:46.170
If you're worried,

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:48.410
call Kaede-san later.

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:49.230
Sure!

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:52.240
<i>I'm so glad I spoke up about it!</i>

00:07:52.710 --> 00:07:56.490
Hinata, Kokona-chan... sorry to bother you.

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:58.490
And thank you!

00:07:58.690 --> 00:07:59.500
Sure!

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:15.160
I've finished getting ready,

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:17.310
but I'm still worried.

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:22.640
Aoi-chan?

00:08:23.010 --> 00:08:24.870
Hello, Kaede-san?

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:25.690
What's wrong?

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:29.040
<i>I forgot to think of what to say.</i>

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:30.660
<i>What'll I do?</i>

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:34.090
You're worried about tomorrow, right?

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:36.450
Uh, right!

00:08:36.850 --> 00:08:39.570
Is it really okay for me to do this?

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:43.230
I was all gung-ho about us going to Mt. Fuji,

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:47.460
but now I've gotten worried about whether 
I'll be able to make it the whole way.

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:51.880
We don't know whether or not 
you'll be able to handle the climb.

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:56.550
I used to go on recklessly tough climbs myself.

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:59.310
I made lots of mistakes and wore myself out.

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:03.560
I often thought, "Enough! 
I'm not doing this again!"

00:09:03.950 --> 00:09:07.110
But later, I still felt like climbing again.

00:09:07.660 --> 00:09:08.560
Probably...

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:11.410
since it was my own decision 
and my own challenge,

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:14.860
I got to reap my own rewards.

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:20.150
Aoi-chan, did you know?

00:09:20.550 --> 00:09:24.120
It's only the lovely memories that remain.

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:27.720
The painful memories go away as time passes,

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:30.130
leaving behind only the lovely ones.

00:09:30.890 --> 00:09:35.960
And so, you need to do your best 
to get those lovely memories.

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:38.510
I need to do my best...

00:09:39.490 --> 00:09:43.890
I think you should probably 
treasure that momentum.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:48.110
For now, if things get dangerous, it's fine 
if we need to turn back partway through.

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:50.810
Try your best to make it eventually.

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:52.620
<i>That's right...</i>

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:56.400
<i>For the first time...</i>

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:01.120
<i>I have some idea of how to tackle 
my fears without giving in to them.</i>

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:04.120
<i>For now, I'll move forward...</i>

00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:08.590
<i>and think on it after tackling it.</i>

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:11.880
Thank you very much, Kaede-san.

00:10:12.390 --> 00:10:14.500
I feel a little better now.

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:16.740
Thank goodness.

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:19.060
Tomorrow will be tough if you're sleep-deprived,

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:20.800
so get plenty of sleep tonight!

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:22.010
Right!

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:23.830
Well, good night!

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:24.850
Good night!

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:27.480
<i>I finally go to Mt. Fuji tomorrow!</i>

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:30.810
<i>What could be waiting for me there?</i>

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:36.730
<i>There's anxiety, and expectation, and other 
feelings I can't quite name, but it's still fun.</i>

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:45.560
I'm too excited to sleep...

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:48.770
One sheep...

00:10:48.770 --> 00:10:50.840
Two sheep...

00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:52.750
Three sheep...

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:57.300
Be careful, Aoi.

00:10:57.470 --> 00:10:58.680
Okay.

00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:00.170
Don't overdo it.

00:11:00.170 --> 00:11:01.510
I know.

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:03.310
I'll be back!

00:11:03.310 --> 00:11:05.010
Make sure to call, okay?

00:11:07.900 --> 00:11:10.150
What time did I fall asleep?

00:11:10.150 --> 00:11:15.400
I remember counting to 125,752 sheep...

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:18.550
Aoi!

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:19.820
Good morning!

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:23.410
<i>We took the Seibu Ikebukuro line to Ikebukuro,</i>

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:26.910
<i>then from Ikebukuro to Shinjuku 
on the Yamanote Line.</i>

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:31.410
<i>And then, we reached the bus terminal 
at the west entrance of Shinjuku station.</i>

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:34.000
Boarding For Nighttime Highway Busses

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:34.000
I bought the tickets!

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:36.750
<i>We've boarded a highway bus,</i>

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:39.760
<i>and are finally headed towards Mt. Fuji.</i>

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:43.900
<i>As we progress down the highway, 
leaving the skyscrapers behind,</i>

00:11:43.900 --> 00:11:45.930
<i>I see fewer and fewer buildings.</i>

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:48.510
Brown Sugar Puffs

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:47.330
<i>And soon...</i>

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:55.980
<i>We will be challenging the 
Mt. Fuji of my dreams!</i>

00:11:57.800 --> 00:11:59.980
To Be Continued!
